---
import Entry from '../../../../layouts/Entry.astro';
import { url } from '../../../../lib/site';
import manifest from '../../../../../public/data/funding-flows/slovenia-dohodnina-1-percent/manifest.json';
import regManifest from '../../../../../public/data/charity-registry/slovenia/manifest.json';
import '../../../../styles/charity-financial-search.css';

const title = 'Slovenia 1% personal income-tax assignments (2019–2025)';
const asset = '/data/funding-flows/slovenia-dohodnina-1-percent/';
const count = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const eurM = (value: number) => `EUR ${(value / 1e6).toFixed(2)}M`;
const eurExact = (value: number) =>
  `EUR ${value.toLocaleString('en-US', { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 })}`;

const sources = [
  {
    title: 'FURS — Seznam prejemnikov za leto 2025 (preliminarni podatki, XLSX)',
    publisher: manifest.publisher,
    url: regManifest.catalogues.furs2025Xlsx,
  },
  {
    title: 'FURS — Seznam prejemnikov za leto 2024 (preliminarni podatki, XLSX)',
    publisher: manifest.publisher,
    url: regManifest.catalogues.furs2024Xlsx,
  },
  {
    title: 'OPSI — Prejemniki namenitve dela dohodnine za donacije (2019–2023 XLSX archive)',
    publisher: 'Open Data of Slovenia (OPSI / FURS)',
    url: regManifest.catalogues.opsiDataset,
  },
  {
    title: 'GOV.SI — Namenitev dela dohodnine za donacije',
    publisher: 'Republic of Slovenia',
    url: regManifest.catalogues.fursDohodninaPortal,
  },
];
---

<Entry
  title={title}
  eyebrow="The Record · Funding Flows · Slovenia"
  summary="Track EUR 93.47M in Slovenian 1% personal income-tax assignments across 7 tax years (2019–2025) and 4.19M taxpayer choices, showing the +96.5% jump when Slovenia doubled its statutory cap from 0.5% to 1.0% in 2020 and comparing five European tax-assignment systems."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'The Record', href: '/record/' },
    { label: 'Funding Flows', href: '/record/funding-flows/' },
    { label: 'Slovenia 1% income-tax assignments' },
  ]}
  filePath="src/pages/record/funding-flows/slovenia-dohodnina-1-percent/index.astro"
  sources={sources}
>
  <p>
    Across seven consecutive assessment years (<strong>2019–2025</strong>), Slovenian taxpayers directed{' '}
    <strong>{eurM(manifest.sevenYearTotals.disclosedTotalEur)}</strong> (<code>{eurExact(manifest.sevenYearTotals.disclosedTotalEur)}</code>)
    through <strong>{count(manifest.sevenYearTotals.disclosedTaxpayerChoices)} disclosed designations</strong> in the Financial Administration
    of the Republic of Slovenia (<strong>FURS</strong>) <em>namenitev dela dohodnine za donacije</em> mechanism.
    When Parliament doubled the statutory ceiling from <strong>0.5%</strong> to <strong>1.0%</strong> of assessed income tax starting tax year
    2020 (PKP7 / ZDoh-2), average allocation per choice nearly doubled overnight from <strong>EUR 10.98</strong> to{' '}
    <strong>EUR 20.96</strong> and total disclosed payouts surged <strong>+{manifest.sevenYearTotals.rateDoublingJumpPct2019To2020}%</strong>{' '}
    (from <code>EUR 5.43M</code> in 2019 to <code>EUR 10.68M</code> in 2020), reaching <strong>EUR 19.24M</strong> across{' '}
    <strong>737,819 choices</strong> in 2025.
  </p>
  <p>
    To search all <strong>{count(regManifest.counts.includedOrganizations)}</strong> TIN-indexed recipients across 2023–2025, open the paired{' '}
    <a href={url('/record/charity-index/slovenia/')}>Slovenia 1% charity index</a>.
  </p>

  <section
    class="charity-financial-search"
    data-si-flow
    data-base={url(asset)}
    data-manifest={JSON.stringify(manifest)}
    aria-labelledby="si-top-search"
  >
    <h2 id="si-top-search">Explore the Top 250 Slovenian 1% recipients (2025)</h2>
    <p id="si-top-hint">
      Filter the 250 largest 2025 recipients by name or 8-digit TIN (e.g., <code>aed</code>, <code>karitas</code>, <code>zpm</code>,
      <code>rdeci noski</code>, <code>gasilska</code>, <code>53655869</code>) and export as JSON or CSV.
    </p>
    <form aria-describedby="si-top-hint">
      <label for="si-top-query">Recipient name or 8-digit TIN</label>
      <div class="finance-actions">
        <input type="search" id="si-top-query" maxlength="160" autocomplete="off" disabled />
        <button type="submit" class="btn" disabled>Filter Top 250</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" data-clear disabled>Reset</button>
      </div>
    </form>
    <p role="status" data-status>
      Load the Top 250 Slovenian 1% recipients ({(manifest.artifacts.top250.bytes / 1024).toFixed(1)} KB compressed).
    </p>
    <div class="finance-actions">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" data-json disabled>Export displayed rows as JSON</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" data-csv disabled>Export displayed rows as CSV</button>
    </div>
    <ol class="finance-results" data-site-symbol="alpineOnePct" aria-label="Top 250 Slovenian 1% recipients" data-results></ol>
  </section>

  <h2 id="seven-year-series">7-year evolution: 0.5% to 1.0% rate doubling &amp; concentration shift (2019–2025)</h2>
  <p>
    Beyond the 2020 rate-doubling jump, the seven-year series reveals a striking second shift: between 2019 and 2021, Slovenia’s top recipient
    captured around <strong>4%</strong> of all payouts (Top-10: ~16%). From 2022 through 2025, one national cardiovascular-defibrillator campaign
    (<em>Društvo za srčno žilne bolezni AED</em>) climbed to <strong>16.82%</strong> of the entire national pool (<strong>EUR 3.24M</strong> /
    <strong>141,039 choices</strong>), lifting Top-10 concentration from <strong>15.95%</strong> in 2021 to <strong>29.13%</strong> in 2025.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Slovenia 7-year 1% income-tax assignment series" tabindex="0">
    <table class="data si-flow-table">
      <caption>FURS preliminary annual payouts, taxpayer choices, average EUR per choice, and concentration (2019–2025)</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Year</th>
          <th scope="col">Cap</th>
          <th scope="col">Rows (disclosed / &lt;5 redacted)</th>
          <th scope="col">Disclosed choices</th>
          <th scope="col">Disclosed EUR</th>
          <th scope="col">Avg EUR / choice</th>
          <th scope="col">Top-1 / Top-10 / Top-50</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          manifest.annualSeries.map((y) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{y.year}</th>
              <td><code>{y.statutoryCap}</code></td>
              <td>{count(y.totalRows)} ({count(y.disclosedRows)} / {count(y.privacyRedactedRows)})</td>
              <td>{count(y.disclosedTaxpayerChoices)}</td>
              <td>{eurExact(y.disclosedTotalEur)}</td>
              <td>EUR {y.avgEurPerChoice.toFixed(2)}</td>
              <td>{y.top1SharePct.toFixed(2)}% / {y.top10SharePct.toFixed(2)}% / {y.top50SharePct.toFixed(2)}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="europe-tax-assignment-compare">Compare five European statutory tax-assignment systems</h2>
  <p>
    Charitology now tracks five European percentage-of-income-tax charity assignment systems using exact official tax-authority records,
    exposing how statutory design shapes charity fundraising concentration:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Slovenia (this page — 1.0% individual dohodnina, 2025):</strong> Doubling the statutory cap from 0.5% to 1.0% in 2020 lifted
      disclosed payouts +96.5% overnight (reaching <code>EUR 19.24M</code> across <code>737,819</code> choices in 2025), while a single
      national AED campaign drove Top-10 concentration from <code>15.95%</code> (2021) to <code>29.13%</code> (2025). FURS redacts rows with
      fewer than 5 donors.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href={url('/record/funding-flows/italy-five-per-mille/')}>Italy (5‰ / 0.5% IRPEF, AF 2025)</a>:</strong> Europe’s largest
      euro pool (<code>EUR 603.10M</code> across <code>96,059</code> admitted entities and <code>15.56M</code> choices) with{' '}
      <code>28.76%</code> Top-10 concentration led by cancer research and medical/humanitarian NGOs boosted by generic-category pools.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href={url('/record/funding-flows/poland-pit-1-5-percent/')}>Poland (1.5% individual PIT, 2025)</a>:</strong> Patient and
      disability sub-accounts (<em>cel szczegółowy</em>) drive Top-10 concentration to <code>45.69%</code> (<code>PLN 2.61B</code> across{' '}
      <code>9,450</code> funded OPPs), while taxpayer counts omit recipients below 100 donors.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href={url('/record/funding-flows/slovakia-pit-2-percent/')}>Slovakia (2%/3% individual + 1%/2% corporate PIT, 2025)</a>:</strong>{' '}
      Permitting corporate income-tax designations places corporate foundations in 8 of the Top 10 spots, with <code>416</code> <em>Nadácia</em>{' '}
      foundations capturing <code>30.87%</code> of payouts (<code>EUR 107.04M</code> across <code>17,457</code> recipients).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href={url('/record/funding-flows/hungary-szja-1-percent/')}>Hungary (1% civil + 1% church/budget SZJA, 2026)</a>:</strong> Lowest
      Top-10 civil concentration at <code>15.04%</code> (<code>HUF 21.40B</code> across <code>31,299</code> civil recipients, plus{' '}
      <code>HUF 23.95B</code> across <code>186</code> second-1% technical-number recipients), led by independent public-interest newsrooms and
      pediatric/emergency hospital foundations.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="downloads">Downloads, methodology and provenance</h2>
  <p>
    All seven FURS preliminary workbooks (2019–2025) are SHA-256 pinned in <code>src/data/slovenia-index-sources.tsv</code>. Years 2019–2022
    omit the <code>DS_UPR</code> tax-number column and power the national aggregate series above; years 2023–2025 carry 100% modulo-11 valid TINs.
    Withheld <code>manj kot 5</code> rows are counted transparently in annual totals and excluded from disclosed EUR sums rather than imputed.{' '}
    <a class="identity-link" data-source-symbol="document" href={url(asset + 'manifest.json')} download>Download flow manifest (JSON)</a> ·{' '}
    <a class="identity-link" data-source-symbol="table" href={url(asset + manifest.artifacts.annualCsv.path)} download>Download 7-year summary (CSV)</a> ·{' '}
    <a class="identity-link" data-source-symbol="document" href={url('/data/charity-registry/slovenia/anomalies.json')} download>anomalies.json</a>.
  </p>
</Entry>

<style>
  .si-flow-table {
    min-inline-size: 52rem;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { $, h } from '../../../../lib/client/dom';
  import { download, toCsv } from '../../../../lib/client/files';
  import { financialCsvName } from '../../../../lib/client/financial-directory';
  import { loadVerifiedJson, type VerifiedJsonAsset } from '../../../../lib/client/verified-json';

  type TopRow = {
    tin: string;
    name: string;
    altNames: string[];
    norm: string;
    donors2025: number | null;
    eur2025: number | null;
    donors2024: number | null;
    eur2024: number | null;
    donors2023: number | null;
    eur2023: number | null;
    total3yrEur: number | null;
  };
  type FlowManifest = {
    publisher: string;
    capturedOn: string;
    artifacts: {
      top250: VerifiedJsonAsset & { path: string; rows: number };
    };
  };

  const normalize = (value: string) =>
    value
      .toLowerCase()
      .replace(/đ/g, 'dj')
      .normalize('NFKD')
      .replace(/\p{M}/gu, '')
      .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, ' ')
      .trim();

  const fmtEur = (val: number | null) =>
    val === null ? '—' : `EUR ${val.toLocaleString('en-US', { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 })}`;

  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-si-flow]')) {
    const manifest: FlowManifest = JSON.parse(root.dataset.manifest!);
    const base = root.dataset.base!;
    const form = $('form', root) as HTMLFormElement;
    const queryEl = $('#si-top-query', root) as HTMLInputElement;
    const statusEl = $('[data-status]', root);
    const listEl = $('[data-results]', root);
    const clearBtn = $('[data-clear]', root) as HTMLButtonElement;
    const jsonBtn = $('[data-json]', root) as HTMLButtonElement;
    const csvBtn = $('[data-csv]', root) as HTMLButtonElement;
    const submitBtn = $('button[type="submit"]', root) as HTMLButtonElement;

    for (const el of [queryEl, submitBtn, clearBtn]) el.disabled = false;

    let cache: Promise<TopRow[]> | null = null;
    let shown: TopRow[] = [];

    const loadTop = () => {
      if (!cache) {
        const asset = manifest.artifacts.top250;
        cache = loadVerifiedJson(base + asset.path, asset).then((data) => {
          if (!Array.isArray(data) || data.length !== asset.rows) {
            throw new Error('Unexpected Slovenia Top 250 row count.');
          }
          return data as TopRow[];
        });
      }
      return cache;
    };

    const render = (rows: TopRow[], total: number, q: string) => {
      shown = rows;
      listEl.replaceChildren();
      jsonBtn.disabled = rows.length === 0;
      csvBtn.disabled = rows.length === 0;
      if (!rows.length) {
        statusEl.textContent = q ? `No Top 250 recipients matched “${q}”.` : 'No recipients matched.';
        return;
      }
      statusEl.textContent =
        total > rows.length
          ? `Showing the first ${rows.length} of ${total} matching Top 250 recipients.`
          : `Showing ${total} matching Top 250 recipient${total === 1 ? '' : 's'}.`;

      for (const r of rows) {
        listEl.append(
          h(
            'li',
            {},
            h('strong', { lang: 'sl' }, r.name),
            ' ',
            h('code', {}, `SI ${r.tin}`),
            h(
              'div',
              { class: 'note' },
              `2025: ${fmtEur(r.eur2025)} (${(r.donors2025 ?? 0).toLocaleString('en-US')} donors) · 2024: ${fmtEur(r.eur2024)} · 2023: ${fmtEur(r.eur2023)}`,
            ),
          ),
        );
      }
    };

    const runFilter = async () => {
      const rawQ = queryEl.value.trim();
      const normQ = normalize(rawQ);
      const digitsQ = rawQ.replace(/\D+/g, '');
      statusEl.textContent = 'Loading Slovenia Top 250 recipients…';
      try {
        const all = await loadTop();
        const filtered = rawQ
          ? all.filter(
              (r) =>
                (digitsQ && r.tin.includes(digitsQ)) ||
                r.name.toLowerCase().includes(rawQ.toLowerCase()) ||
                (normQ && r.norm.includes(normQ)),
            )
          : all;
        render(filtered.slice(0, 50), filtered.length, rawQ);
      } catch (err) {
        statusEl.textContent = err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Could not load Slovenia Top 250.';
      }
    };

    form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      void runFilter();
    });
    clearBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      queryEl.value = '';
      shown = [];
      listEl.replaceChildren();
      jsonBtn.disabled = true;
      csvBtn.disabled = true;
      statusEl.textContent = 'Filter reset.';
      queryEl.focus();
    });
    jsonBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!shown.length) return;
      download(
        'charitology-slovenia-dohodnina-top250.json',
        JSON.stringify({ source: manifest.publisher, capturedOn: manifest.capturedOn, rows: shown }, null, 2),
        'application/json;charset=utf-8',
      );
    });
    csvBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!shown.length) return;
      const csvText = toCsv(
        shown.map((r) => ({
          tin_ds_upr: r.tin,
          recipient_name: financialCsvName(r.name),
          donors_2025: r.donors2025 ?? '',
          eur_2025: r.eur2025 === null ? '' : r.eur2025.toFixed(2),
          donors_2024: r.donors2024 ?? '',
          eur_2024: r.eur2024 === null ? '' : r.eur2024.toFixed(2),
          donors_2023: r.donors2023 ?? '',
          eur_2023: r.eur2023 === null ? '' : r.eur2023.toFixed(2),
          total_3yr_eur: r.total3yrEur === null ? '' : r.total3yrEur.toFixed(2),
        })),
      );
      download('charitology-slovenia-dohodnina-top250.csv', '\uFEFF' + csvText, 'text/csv;charset=utf-8');
    });
  }
</script>
